The full suite passes: **261 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.

## Summary

The change enforces that an owner's telephone number must be unique across all owners, returning **409 Conflict** on violation.

The infrastructure for this (the `DuplicateOwnerException` → 409 handler in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, and the duplicate check gate in `saveOwner`) was already present from prior work; it previously matched on last name **and** telephone. I broadened the rule to telephone-only:

**`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** — replaced the last-name+telephone check with a telephone-across-all-owners check:
```java
if (owner.isNew() && isDuplicateTelephone(owner)) {
    throw new DuplicateOwnerException(
        "An owner with the same telephone already exists");
}
...
private boolean isDuplicateTelephone(Owner owner) {
    return ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
        .anyMatch(existing -> !existing.getId().equals(owner.getId())
            && Objects.equals(existing.getTelephone(), owner.getTelephone()));
}
```

The check is gated on `owner.isNew()`, so it only applies to creation (as specified) and leaves updates unaffected. I also updated the `DuplicateOwnerException` javadoc to reflect the new rule.

The new acceptance test `Cp03Tests` (duplicate telephone → 409, distinct telephones → 2xx) passes, and the earlier `Cp01`/`Cp02` tests still pass since those scenarios also involve matching telephones.
